## 2026-08-29 — Vibe coder capability layer

- **Decision:** Golden path (`assets/stack-playbooks/golden-path.md`) is **opt-in** when the user has no stack preference — not an automatic default.
- **Why:** Speed for vibe coding without trapping users who named a stack.
- **Alternatives rejected:** Golden path as hard default; stay fully silent with no opinionated option.
- **Revisit when:** Most clones pick the same stack in practice.

- **Decision:** Feature integrations use one `add-integration` skill plus `assets/recipes/*.md`, not six nearly identical skills.
- **Why:** One procedure; stack/vendor detail stays on-demand; Cloud Agents get portable recipes without user-level vendor skills.
- **Alternatives rejected:** One skill per integration; relying only on `~/.cursor` vendor skills.
- **Revisit when:** A recipe grows large enough to need its own skill (migrations already did → `migrate-database`).

- **Decision:** UI polish is a `polish-ui` skill + `assets/checklists/ui-polish.md` (verifiable), with globbed `30-frontend.mdc` for local habits.
- **Why:** Vibe users judge on look/feel; always-apply must stay short.
- **Alternatives rejected:** Dumping a full style guide into always-apply rules.
- **Revisit when:** The product adopts a stricter design system.

## 2026-08-29 — Agent starter hardening

- **Decision:** Boilerplate (CI, GitHub templates, Docker, linters, hooks) stays under `assets/templates/` and is copied on demand — not materialized at repo root.
- **Why:** Keeps the starter stack-agnostic; Cloud and local clones stay blank until bootstrap.
- **Alternatives rejected:** Materializing CI/Docker at root; hybrid root+templates for every file.
- **Revisit when:** The starter itself becomes a product app, or users consistently want default CI at clone time.

- **Decision:** Security is both prose and tooling — `security-review` skill, `security-reviewer` subagent, `20-security.mdc`, checklists, `scripts/scan-secrets.mjs`, and a CI security-scan template.
- **Why:** Agents need a planned review path and a mechanical gate; Cloud Agents cannot rely on user-level security skills.
- **Alternatives rejected:** Checklist-only; tooling-only without a review runbook.
- **Revisit when:** A preferred org-wide scanner replaces the local script.

- **Decision:** Cursor hooks ship as inert templates under `assets/templates/hooks/` (Node `.mjs`), not enabled by default.
- **Why:** Hooks change every agent run; a bad deny rule blocks work. Node scripts are portable to Windows and Linux Cloud Agents (`.sh` is not).
- **Alternatives rejected:** Activating `.cursor/hooks.json` out of the box; shell-only hooks.
- **Revisit when:** The user asks to enable project hooks.

## Template defaults (2026-08-29)

- **Working memory lives in project rules**, not chat and not `~/.cursor`. Cloud Agents only see the repo.
- **Skills for workflows, rules for constraints.** Bootstrap, MCP, and memory updates are skills.
- **MCP is opt-in.** The catalog is in `assets/mcp-catalog.md`. `.cursor/mcp.json` starts empty.
- **No application stack until bootstrap.** Do not assume Next.js, Python, or any framework.

